    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>PlexBlocks – Advanced Tabs for Block Editor adds tab navigation blocks for product details, feature breakdowns, comparisons, FAQs, and compact content sections.</p>\n<p>Included blocks:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Advanced Tabs</li>\n<li>Tab Panel</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>accessible tab navigation</li>\n<li>horizontal and vertical layouts</li>\n<li>URL hash support</li>\n<li>optional mobile accordion mode</li>\n<li>per-block styling controls</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Developer Credits</h3>\n<p>This plugin was developed by ConicPlex, a leading agency specializing in WordPress plugin development. For more information about ConicPlex and their services, visit <a href=\"https://conicplex.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a>.</p>\n<h3>Credits &amp; 3rd Party Services</h3>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex.com</a></strong>: PlexBlocks – Advanced Tabs for Block Editor uses <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a> (own website) to store plugin insights. Whenever the plugin is activated, deactivated, or uninstalled, an API request is sent to Conicplex to record the action. The API request includes the action, site URL, admin email, plugin version, plugin name, plugin text domain, WordPress version, site language, and site timezone. <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/privacy-policy/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/terms-conditions/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the WordPress admin.</li>\n<li>Insert the <code>Advanced Tabs</code> block in the block editor.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"can%20i%20deep-link%20to%20a%20tab%3F\">\nCan I deep-link to a tab?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. The block supports hash-based tab navigation.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20support%20mobile-friendly%20layouts%3F\">\nDoes it support mobile-friendly layouts?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. It includes an optional mobile accordion pattern.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Create accessible tabbed content layouts in the WordPress block editor.",
    "description": "<p>PlexBlocks – Advanced Tabs for Block Editor adds tab navigation blocks for product details, feature breakdowns, comparisons, FAQs, and compact content sections.</p>\n<p>Included blocks:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Advanced Tabs</li>\n<li>Tab Panel</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>accessible tab navigation</li>\n<li>horizontal and vertical layouts</li>\n<li>URL hash support</li>\n<li>optional mobile accordion mode</li>\n<li>per-block styling controls</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Developer Credits</h3>\n<p>This plugin was developed by ConicPlex, a leading agency specializing in WordPress plugin development. For more information about ConicPlex and their services, visit <a href=\"https://conicplex.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a>.</p>\n<h3>Credits &amp; 3rd Party Services</h3>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex.com</a></strong>: PlexBlocks – Advanced Tabs for Block Editor uses <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a> (own website) to store plugin insights. Whenever the plugin is activated, deactivated, or uninstalled, an API request is sent to Conicplex to record the action. The API request includes the action, site URL, admin email, plugin version, plugin name, plugin text domain, WordPress version, site language, and site timezone. <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/privacy-policy/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/terms-conditions/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</p>\n",
